{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:72-74` says the review-bot image installs the `nava-rebar[agents]` extra with `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]`. `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:211-215` says the compose stack runs two containers, Gerrit and review-bot, and repeats the `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` install shape.\n\nThe current image build uses locked uv, not a bare pip install. `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:93-100` pins uv through `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.7` and runs `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock`; `pyproject.toml:353-356` pins `[tool.uv] required-version = \"==0.12.7\"`.\n\nThe current compose file defines four services, not two: `gerrit` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:27`, `review-bot` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:76`, `opcert` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:346`, and `mcp` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:418`. nginx remains host-side and outside compose; the service comments describe host nginx proxying to the loopback-published service ports at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:37-38`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:279-280`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:394-395`, and `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:407-410`.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` to match the current review-bot Dockerfile and compose topology. Leave historical ADR prose unchanged unless the referenced lines are part of the operator guide statements above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` removes the review-bot prerequisite claim at lines 72-74 that the image bakes `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` and replaces it with the locked install from `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:98-100`: uv `0.12.7` running `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock`.\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` replaces the repeated `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` claim at line 213 with the same locked uv install and mentions that `pyproject.toml:353-356` pins the required uv version to `==0.12.7`.\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` removes the two-container topology claim at lines 211-212 and replaces it with the four compose services from `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: `gerrit`, `review-bot`, `opcert`, and `mcp`.\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` keeps nginx described as host-side and outside compose, with nginx proxying to loopback-published service ports rather than listed as a compose service.\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` leaves historical ADR 0007 wording unchanged outside the current operator-guide drift at lines 72-74 and 211-215.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0 after the documentation edit.\n\n## Testing\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` from the repository checkout and land only if it exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789871473432736268,"uuid":"172994b4-0205-4af6-b12d-b95cee16b962"}